ntil-5-17 | [^<l] until-5\nuntil-5-17 ::= | [<] until-5-01 | [^<>] until-5\n","grammar_lazy":false,"grammar_triggers":[],"preserved_tokens":[248058,248059,248068,248069],"chat_format":"peg-native","reasoning_format":"deepseek","reasoning_in_content":false,"generation_prompt":"<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","samplers":["penalties","dry","top_n_sigma","top_k","typ_p","top_p","min_p","xtc","temperature"],"speculative.types":"none","timings_per_token":false,"post_sampling_probs":false,"backend_sampling":false,"lora":[]},"next_token":[{"has_next_token":false,"has_new_line":false,"n_remain":-1,"n_decoded":0}],"prompt":"<|im_start|>system\n# Bluehaven bounded-work actor\n\nYou operate against an exact externally custodied world. Use only declared\nactions and return exactly one JSON action object. Source observations,\ncandidate effects, checks, and rejection receipts are exact. Receipts preserve\nidentity and reopenability but not source meaning.\n\nYour objective is useful completion: produce a source-correct water-restoration\npackage, incorporate effects, obtain a current check, repair defects, recheck,\nand propose submission only after a current check and after you can identify no\nconcrete unresolved task requirement. The external candidate-bound evaluator,\nnot the actor, assigns final readiness. Citation breadth, a model-authored\nledger, a green stale check, or submission itself is not readiness authority.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Task: Bluehaven drinking-water restoration package\n\nA river contamination event, power instability, and distribution constraints\nthreaten Bluehaven's drinking-water system. Produce two exact deliverables:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`\n\nThe fixed second filename is imposed by the runtime; its content is an\noperational drinking-water restoration decision. Reconcile the complete system\nover seventy-two hours rather than summarizing sources independently.\n\n## Evidence-ledger contract\n\nBegin with `# Evidence Integration Ledger` and maintain entries `R01` through\n`R12`. Each entry must state a disposition, cite only exact observed sources as\n`[SNN]`, preserve units, probabilities, revisions, conflicts and\nqualifications, bind current or missing evidence, and name blockers. The ledger\nis model-authored, lossy task work and never readiness authority.\n\n## Decision-document contract\n\nBegin with `# Bluehaven Drinking-Water Restoration Decision` and use exactly\nthese level-two headings in this order:\n\n1. `## Decision, scope, and authority`\n2. `## Contamination triggers and service-zone sequencing`\n3. `## Demand, treatment, and distribution capacity`\n4. `## Critical customers and alternate-water continuity`\n5. `## Power, staffing, logistics, and mutual aid`\n6. `## Public warning, sampling, and accountability`\n7. `## Seventy-two-hour execution and contingencies`\n8. `## Verification, readiness, blockers, and falsifiers`\n\nWrite 1,400–2,000 words excluding exact citations. Cite at least twelve unique\nsources and include S01–S11 and S13–S16.\n\nResolve these coupled requirements:\n\n- `R01`: recommendation, public-health order, operations, checking, handoff,\n  cost escalation, and closure authority;\n- `R02`: exact residual and benzene triggers, conservative plume branch,\n  hold/lift observations, expiry, and common forecast/sample/action binding;\n- `R03`: population and time-bound potable demand, overlapping vulnerability,\n  registry coverage, uncovered-population uncertainty, loss, and critical demand;\n- `R04`: shared East-trunk treatment limit, observed output, hydraulic delivery,\n  pressure, valve/pump effects, and current capacity proof;\n- `R05`: hospitals, dialysis, care facilities, accessible/private matching,\n  potable specifications, handoffs, and blocking thresholds;\n- `R06`: certified tanker and bottle capacity, staffed cycles, activation,\n  disinfection, shared loading assets, road/vendor constraints, and relief;\n- `R07`: generator endurance, observed fuel delay, local staging or alternate\n  supply, laboratory power, staffing qualifications, duty, and safety;\n- `R08`: multilingual redundant warning, outage-aware reach, door-knock time,\n  exact revision, receipt/understanding evidence, and correction;\n- `R09`: sample locations, custody, quality control, six/nine-hour assays, two\n  clean rounds, candidate currency, and release authority;\n- `R10`: private accountability, public aggregation, verified self-supply,\n  restricted clinical data, reconciliation, seven/thirty-day retention, and\n  deletion proof;\n- `R11`: executable seventy-two-hour sequence with owners, resources, effects,\n  current checks, repair, recheck, cost authority, and contingencies; and\n- `R12`: every exercise and independent-review blocker, source uncertainty,\n  candidate-bound readiness, explicit falsifiers, and correct closure.\n\nPreserve source distinctions exactly. In particular, do not convert a\nchemical threshold into a duration or flow, a forecast probability into a\nphysical measurement or demand estimate, registry coverage into demand\nreduction, a shared bottleneck into summed capacity, a common revision binding\ninto a count of permitted changes, or a contractual target into observed\nperformance. Recover the exact values and qualifications from the source\nrecord rather than treating this task statement as evidence.\n\nAlso preserve that:\n\n- owner attestation, component dashboards, stale checks, ledgers, and\n  submission are not readiness proof.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Ordinary actor actions\n\nReturn exactly one JSON object and no surrounding prose.\n\n- `{\"action\":\"read_source\",\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":70}`\n- `{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":70},{\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"start_line\":1,\"end_line\":70}]}`\n- `{\"action\":\"reopen_exact\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"replace_evidence_ledger\",\"content\":\"# Evidence Integration Ledger\\n...\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"upsert_decision_section\",\"heading\":\"Decision, scope, and authority\",\"body\":\"...\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"replace_decision\",\"content\":\"# Bluehaven Drinking-Water Restoration Decision\\n...\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"run_check\"}`\n- `{\"action\":\"submit\"}`\n\nOne source range is at most 120 lines. A batch contains at most two\nnon-overlapping ranges, 160 total lines, 12,000 exact source bytes, and a 6,500\ntoken model-visible result. The same result cap applies to a single read.\nCandidate effects invalidate checks of an earlier candidate. A check result\nalways names the exact candidate it evaluated and whether that result is\ncurrent for the presently visible candidate.\n\n\n# Exact source catalog\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-source-catalog-v0\",\"sources\":[{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"c90f647766613d6e81f7cb2f7a2738bf3119e90ca8385ba3b2d7b9fadc4f7685\",\"size_bytes\":4182,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"title\":\"Bluehaven emergency drinking-water authority\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"2271ec6007702903ad1c4dcecd819c4ec176e7345a0323c2bbe47e00954ade0c\",\"size_bytes\":3707,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"title\":\"Contamination thresholds and conservative response triggers\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"542346c71ea244ed887ad9fa9e4901722fdfc2f67cd629cec2503f4f964f30b5\",\"size_bytes\":4204,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"title\":\"Service-zone demand, registry coverage, and vulnerable households\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"31775314f25121b2200159075bc3c4035b479973fad09eb9b60ac8d8ca604e41\",\"size_bytes\":4042,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"title\":\"Treatment-plant capacity and shared clearwell limits\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"e8a4909318ffa921eb6eecab365943dc47bb95f246683043be9a4897b047f411\",\"size_bytes\":3529,\"source_id\":\"S05\",\"title\":\"Distribution hydraulics, pressure zones, and isolation effects\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha2