,\"title\":\"River plume ensemble and common revision cadence\"},{\"line_count\":70,\"sha256\":\"5354e82174a5bc59e57482b535ac1df2aa2064f63c561f2b94569adea36cf494\",\"size_bytes\":4207,\"source_id\":\"S16\",\"title\":\"Independent Bluehaven restoration-readiness review\"}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n# Exact current candidate\n{\"candidate_sha256\":\"8d31af5fb5ce89321c8b02a3e7a4e8264f5486d8cb13d3d5298a31f13a9a0250\",\"candidate_version\":\"candidate-v000:8d31af5fb5ce89321c8b02a3e7a4e8264f5486d8cb13d3d5298a31f13a9a0250\",\"files\":{\"BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md\":\"6e69a4d89c7ff8b040c4b619ca394d3a1bf10548d4539927c0f38d907f8b6832\",\"EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md\":\"805bd2bf2bbe6ed48d6d6e68a4417475fd48db9e12c01440afb4b52c37e9fb23\"},\"schema\":\"architecture-current-candidate-v0\"}\n--- exact candidate file: EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md ---\n# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\nR01–R12 are unresolved. No exact source observation has yet been integrated.\n\n--- exact candidate file: BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md ---\n# Bluehaven Drinking-Water Restoration Decision\n\nNo source-grounded restoration decision has been constructed.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"start_line\":1}]\n}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S01:1-70+S02:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"6ead1f44b5f6c472ff68cda7d53c92ed8aa4c5eca9ad213830ab81c5fc8cd6bb\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8341}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S01\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S01_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"c90f647766613d6e81f7cb2f7a2738bf3119e90ca8385ba3b2d7b9fadc4f7685\",\"source_size_bytes\":4182,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Bluehaven emergency drinking-water authority\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe public-health officer issues or lifts a boil-water order after the utility laboratory recommendation. The utility director owns operational restoration; neither a vendor nor a dashboard can declare public-health readiness.\nThe operations chief may isolate mains and dispatch tankers, while the mayor controls emergency expenditure above the utility director's delegated ceiling. These roles are distinct.\nA shift handoff is valid only when the receiving officer acknowledges the same incident-plan and water-quality revision. An unacknowledged transfer blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTrigger evidence from S02 and S15 informs the health officer but does not replace the legal order. Restoration effects require a current laboratory and hydraulic check.\nEvery public notice, field action, and checker must bind the same incident revision and effective time.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUTH-000 | utility-director | r2 | 1.0 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-001 | health-officer | r2 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-002 | operations-chief | r2 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-003 | mayor | r2 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-004 | utility-director | r2 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-005 | health-officer | r2 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-006 | operations-chief | r2 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-007 | mayor | r2 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-008 | utility-director | r2 | 3.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-009 | health-officer | r2 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-010 | operations-chief | r2 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-011 | mayor | r2 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-012 | utility-director | r2 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-013 | health-officer | r2 | 3.9 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-014 | operations-chief | r2 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-015 | mayor | r2 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-016 | utility-director | r3 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-017 | health-officer | r3 | 3.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-018 | operations-chief | r3 | 1.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-019 | mayor | r3 | 1.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-020 | utility-director | r3 | 2.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-021 | health-officer | r3 | 3.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-022 | operations-chief | r3 | 4.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-023 | mayor | r3 | 1.6 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-024 | utility-director | r3 | 2.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-025 | health-officer | r3 | 3.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-026 | operations-chief | r3 | 3.7 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-027 | mayor | r3 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-028 | utility-director | r3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-029 | health-officer | r3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-030 | operations-chief | r3 | 3.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-031 | mayor | r3 | 1.0 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-032 | utility-director | r4 | 1.7 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-033 | health-officer | r4 | 2.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-034 | operations-chief | r4 | 3.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-035 | mayor | r4 | 3.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-036 | utility-director | r4 | 1.4 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-037 | health-officer | r4 | 2.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-038 | operations-chief | r4 | 2.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-039 | mayor | r4 | 3.5 | approval | hold |\n| AUTH-040 | utility-director | r4 | 1.1 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-041 | health-officer | r4 | 1.8 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-042 | operations-chief | r4 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-043 | mayor | r4 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-044 | utility-director | r4 | 3.9 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-045 | health-officer | r4 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-046 | operations-chief | r4 | 2.2 | approval | current |\n| AUTH-047 | mayor | r4 | 2.9 | approval | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nDistinguish recommendation, legal order, operational execution, verification, and closure authority.\nDo not treat a model-authored ledger, vendor assertion, or submission as readiness authority.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S02\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S02_CONTAMINATION.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"2271ec6007702903ad1c4dcecd819c4ec176e7345a0323c2bbe47e00954ade0c\",\"source_size_bytes\":3707,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Contamination thresholds and conservative response triggers\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nA mandatory boil-water order begins when treated chlorine residual remains below 0.2 mg/L in two consecutive validated samples or when benzene exceeds 5 micrograms per liter in any confirmed distribution sample.\nThe median plume forecast stays north of the intake, but 38 percent of current ensemble members reverse after 18:00. The conservative branch governs intake isolation until field samples rule it out.\nOne clean sample cannot cancel an active order. Lifting requires two compliant rounds, hydraulic stabilization, and public-health approval.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nDemand and alternate-water supply from S03 and S08 must cover the period implied by laboratory turnaround in S09, not only pipe travel time.\nRiver forecast revision in S15, treatment state in S04, and public notice in S10 must remain on one candidate-bound revision.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| WQ-000 | North-intake | r2 | 0.2 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-001 | East-clearwell | r2 | 0.9 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-002 | Zone-A | r2 | 1.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-003 | Zone-B | r2 | 2.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-004 | North-intake | r2 | 3.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-005 | East-clearwell | r2 | 0.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-006 | Zone-A | r2 | 1.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-007 | Zone-B | r2 | 2.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-008 | North-intake | r2 | 2.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-009 | East-clearwell | r2 | 0.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-010 | Zone-A | r2 | 1.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-011 | Zone-B | r2 | 1.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-012 | North-intake | r2 | 2.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-013 | East-clearwell | r2 | 3.1 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-014 | Zone-A | r2 | 0.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-015 | Zone-B | r2 | 1.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-016 | North-intake | r3 | 2.1 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-017 | East-clearwell | r3 | 2.8 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-018 | Zone-A | r3 | 0.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-019 | Zone-B | r3 | 1.1 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-020 | North-intake | r3 | 1.8 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-021 | East-clearwell | r3 | 2.5 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-022 | Zone-A | r3 | 3.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-023 | Zone-B | r3 | 0.8 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-024 | North-intake | r3 | 1.5 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-025 | East-clearwell | r3 | 2.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-026 | Zone-A | r3 | 2.9 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-027 | Zone-B | r3 | 0.5 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-028 | North-intake | r3 | 1.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-029 | East-clearwell | r3 | 1.9 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-030 | Zone-A | r3 | 2.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-031 | Zone-B | r3 | 0.2 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-032 | North-intake | r4 | 0.9 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-033 | East-clearwell | r4 | 1.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-034 | Zone-A | r4 | 2.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-035 | Zone-B | r4 | 3.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-036 | North-intake | r4 | 0.6 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-037 | East-clearwell | r4 | 1.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-038 | Zone-A | r4 | 2.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-039 | Zone-B | r4 | 2.7 | mg/L | hold |\n| WQ-040 | North-intake | r4 | 0.3 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-041 | East-clearwell | r4 | 1.0 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-042 | Zone-A | r4 | 1.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-043 | Zone-B | r4 | 2.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-044 | North-intake | r4 | 3.1 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-045 | East-clearwell | r4 | 0.7 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-046 | Zone-A | r4 | 1.4 | mg/L | current |\n| WQ-047 | Zone-B | r4 | 2.1 | mg/L | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nPreserve 0.2 mg/L, 5 micrograms per liter, and 38 percent with their exact meanings and units.\nState the observations that start, hold, expand, and lift each protective action.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n{\"action\":\"read_batch\",\"requests\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"start_line\":1}]}<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>user\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:S03:1-70+S04:1-70\",\"object_version\":\"55d17ff7177afbe97753425481cc305623d764d31a0c72fecb1db120c87f8ce2\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-002\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8691}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S03\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S03_DEMAND.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"542346c71ea244ed887ad9fa9e4901722fdfc2f67cd629cec2503f4f964f30b5\",\"source_size_bytes\":4204,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Service-zone demand, registry coverage, and vulnerable households\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nBluehaven serves 46,800 residents: 8,200 in Zone A, 12,600 in B, 15,400 in C, and 10,600 in D. Daytime industrial demand adds 2.4 megaliters per day but is not drinking-water demand.\nThe emergency minimum is three liters per person per day plus separately calculated clinical and sanitation demand. Vulnerability categories overlap and cannot be summed as independent people.\nThe customer and meter registry covers 94 percent of occupied premises. The uncovered six percent requires an uncertainty allowance; it is not a six-percent reduction in demand.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nTreatment and distribution capacity in S04-S05 must be compared with time-bound potable demand after losses, not with nominal plant nameplate totals.\nCritical facilities in S07 and tanker logistics in S08 need explicit priority allocations outside the household minimum.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| DEM-000 | Zone-A | r2 | 46.8 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-001 | Zone-B | r2 | 47.5 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-002 | Zone-C | r2 | 48.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-003 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-004 | Zone-A | r2 | 49.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-005 | Zone-B | r2 | 47.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-006 | Zone-C | r2 | 47.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-007 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-008 | Zone-A | r2 | 49.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-009 | Zone-B | r2 | 46.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-010 | Zone-C | r2 | 47.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-011 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-012 | Zone-A | r2 | 49.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-013 | Zone-B | r2 | 49.7 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-014 | Zone-C | r2 | 47.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-015 | Zone-D | r2 | 48.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-016 | Zone-A | r3 | 48.7 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-017 | Zone-B | r3 | 49.4 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-018 | Zone-C | r3 | 47.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-019 | Zone-D | r3 | 47.7 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-020 | Zone-A | r3 | 48.4 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-021 | Zone-B | r3 | 49.1 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-022 | Zone-C | r3 | 49.8 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-023 | Zone-D | r3 | 47.4 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-024 | Zone-A | r3 | 48.1 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-025 | Zone-B | r3 | 48.8 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-026 | Zone-C | r3 | 49.5 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-027 | Zone-D | r3 | 47.1 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-028 | Zone-A | r3 | 47.8 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-029 | Zone-B | r3 | 48.5 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-030 | Zone-C | r3 | 49.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-031 | Zone-D | r3 | 46.8 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-032 | Zone-A | r4 | 47.5 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-033 | Zone-B | r4 | 48.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-034 | Zone-C | r4 | 48.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-035 | Zone-D | r4 | 49.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-036 | Zone-A | r4 | 47.2 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-037 | Zone-B | r4 | 47.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-038 | Zone-C | r4 | 48.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-039 | Zone-D | r4 | 49.3 | thousand-people | hold |\n| DEM-040 | Zone-A | r4 | 46.9 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-041 | Zone-B | r4 | 47.6 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-042 | Zone-C | r4 | 48.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-043 | Zone-D | r4 | 49.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-044 | Zone-A | r4 | 49.7 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-045 | Zone-B | r4 | 47.3 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-046 | Zone-C | r4 | 48.0 | thousand-people | current |\n| DEM-047 | Zone-D | r4 | 48.7 | thousand-people | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nState population basis, overlap rule, registry uncertainty, loss allowance, and time-bound demand.\nDo not convert 94 percent coverage into a 94 percent readiness score or six percent into a demand target.\n--- exact batch segment 2 ---\n{\"end_line\":70,\"source_id\":\"S04\",\"source_path\":\"sources/S04_TREATMENT.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"31775314f25121b2200159075bc3c4035b479973fad09eb9b60ac8d8ca604e41\",\"source_size_bytes\":4042,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Treatment-plant capacity and shared clearwell limits\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nPlant A is rated at 12 megaliters per day and Plant B at 9, but both discharge through the East clearwell and trunk whose validated sustainable limit is 15 megaliters per day. The ratings cannot be added to claim 21.\nThe last integrated run sustained 13.4 megaliters per day after filter backwash and distribution losses. A higher figure requires a current candidate-bound test.\nPlant B cannot treat the benzene branch without the mobile carbon unit, whose activation and staffing are governed by S12.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nHydraulic zone pressure in S05 can reduce deliverable potable capacity below treatment output. Generator state in S06 constrains both plants and the shared clearwell pumps.\nAlternate-water obligations in S08 are the gap between validated delivered capacity and demand, not the gap from nameplate output.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| PLANT-000 | Plant-A | r2 | 13.4 | ML/day | hold |\n| PLANT-001 | Plant-B | r2 | 14.1 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-002 | East-clearwell | r2 | 14.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-003 | West-clearwell | r2 | 15.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-004 | Plant-A | r2 | 16.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-005 | Plant-B | r2 | 13.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-006 | East-clearwell | r2 | 14.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-007 | West-clearwell | r2 | 15.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-008 | Plant-A | r2 | 15.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-009 | Plant-B | r2 | 13.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-010 | East-clearwell | r2 | 14.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-011 | West-clearwell | r2 | 14.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-012 | Plant-A | r2 | 15.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-013 | Plant-B | r2 | 16.3 | ML/day | hold |\n| PLANT-014 | East-clearwell | r2 | 13.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-015 | West-clearwell | r2 | 14.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-016 | Plant-A | r3 | 15.3 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-017 | Plant-B | r3 | 16.0 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-018 | East-clearwell | r3 | 13.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-019 | West-clearwell | r3 | 14.3 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-020 | Plant-A | r3 | 15.0 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-021 | Plant-B | r3 | 15.7 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-022 | East-clearwell | r3 | 16.4 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-023 | West-clearwell | r3 | 14.0 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-024 | Plant-A | r3 | 14.7 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-025 | Plant-B | r3 | 15.4 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-026 | East-clearwell | r3 | 16.1 | ML/day | hold |\n| PLANT-027 | West-clearwell | r3 | 13.7 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-028 | Plant-A | r3 | 14.4 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-029 | Plant-B | r3 | 15.1 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-030 | East-clearwell | r3 | 15.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-031 | West-clearwell | r3 | 13.4 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-032 | Plant-A | r4 | 14.1 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-033 | Plant-B | r4 | 14.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-034 | East-clearwell | r4 | 15.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-035 | West-clearwell | r4 | 16.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-036 | Plant-A | r4 | 13.8 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-037 | Plant-B | r4 | 14.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-038 | East-clearwell | r4 | 15.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-039 | West-clearwell | r4 | 15.9 | ML/day | hold |\n| PLANT-040 | Plant-A | r4 | 13.5 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-041 | Plant-B | r4 | 14.2 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-042 | East-clearwell | r4 | 14.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-043 | West-clearwell | r4 | 15.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-044 | Plant-A | r4 | 16.3 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-045 | Plant-B | r4 | 13.9 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-046 | East-clearwell | r4 | 14.6 | ML/day | current |\n| PLANT-047 | West-clearwell | r4 | 15.3 | ML/day | current |\n\n## Decision constraints\n\nUse the shared 15 ML/day bottleneck and observed 13.4 ML/day until a current integrated test proves more.\nBind treatment mode, carbon unit, power, staffing, loss, and hydraulic effects together.<|im_end|>\n<|im_start|>assistant\n<think>\n\n</think>\n\n","generated":""}
