er cycle; only five qualified drivers can report within two hours. A full clean-load-deliver-disinfect cycle averages 4.5 hours.\nThe bottling contract supplies 110,000 liters per day after a ten-hour activation delay. Two listed tanker vendors carry nonpotable construction tanks and cannot serve drinking water.\nLoading Bay 2 shares power and pumps with Plant A. Counting plant output and tanker loading independently double-counts the same constrained asset.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nHousehold demand in S03, clinical priority in S07, plant/power state in S04/S06, and road access in S12 determine usable alternate-water throughput.\nDriver duty and disinfection time require relief capacity; nominal tank volume is not sustained daily delivery.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | revision | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| ALT-000 | tanker | r2 | 5.6 | ML/day | hold |\n| ALT-001 | bottle-line | r2 | 6.3 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-002 | loading-bay | r2 | 7.0 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-003 | distribution-point | r2 | 7.7 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-004 | tanker | r2 | 8.4 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-005 | bottle-line | r2 | 6.0 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-006 | loading-bay | r2 | 6.7 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-007 | distribution-point | r2 | 7.4 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-008 | tanker | r2 | 8.1 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-009 | bottle-line | r2 | 5.7 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-010 | loading-bay | r2 | 6.4 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-011 | distribution-point | r2 | 7.1 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-012 | tanker | r2 | 7.8 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-013 | bottle-line | r2 | 8.5 | ML/day | hold |\n| ALT-014 | loading-bay | r2 | 6.1 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-015 | distribution-point | r2 | 6.8 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-016 | tanker | r3 | 7.5 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-017 | bottle-line | r3 | 8.2 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-018 | loading-bay | r3 | 5.8 | ML/day | current |\n| ALT-019 | distribution-point | r3 | 6.5 